   "source": [
    "# JEV Engineering: Joint Embedding Vector Context Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "This Jupyter notebook provides comprehensive insights into JEV (Joint Embedding Vector) Engineering, a cutting-edge approach to LLM context optimization and augmentation that combines embedding techniques with advanced vector manipulation for enhanced language model performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Understanding JEV Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "**JEV Engineering** represents a sophisticated approach to context optimization that leverages joint embedding techniques to create more effective context windows for language models. It combines the power of embeddings with engineered context structures to maximize model performance and understanding."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Core JEV Engineering Principles\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Joint Embedding Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept**: JEV creates unified embedding spaces that combine multiple input modalities into a single coherent representation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Techniques**:\n",
    "- Multi-modal fusion embeddings\n",
    "- Cross-modal attention mechanisms\n",
    "- Unified vector space optimization\n",
    "- Context-aware embedding generation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Implementation**:\n",
    "```python\n# Joint Embedding Vector - Basic Implementation\nclass JointEmbeddingVector:\n    def __init__(self, embedding_dim=768, context_window=8192):\n        self.embedding_dim = embedding_dim\n        self.context_window = context_window\n        self.text_encoder = TextEncoder(embedding_dim)\n        self.vision_encoder = VisionEncoder(embedding_dim)\n        self.audio_encoder = AudioEncoder(embedding_dim)\n        self.fusion_layer = CrossModalFusion(embedding_dim)\n    \n    def create_joint_context(self, inputs, fusion_strategy='concat'):\n        # Encode different modalities\n        text_embeddings = self.text_encoder.encode(inputs['text'])
        vision_embeddings = self.vision_encoder.encode(inputs['vision']) if 'vision' in inputs else None
        audio_embeddings = self.audio_encoder.encode(inputs['audio']) if 'audio' in inputs else None
        \n        # Apply fusion strategy\n        if fusion_strategy == 'concat':\n            joint_embedding = self._concat_fusion(text_embeddings, vision_embeddings, audio_embeddings)
        elif fusion_strategy == 'attention':\n            joint_embedding = self._attention_fusion(text_embeddings, vision_embeddings, audio_embeddings)
        elif fusion_strategy == 'bilinear':\n            joint_embedding = self._bilinear_fusion(text_embeddings, vision_embeddings, audio_embeddings)
        \n        return self._optimize_context_window(joint_embedding)\n    \n    def _concat_fusion(self, text_emb, vision_emb, audio_emb):\n        # Simple concatenation approach\n        embeddings = [text_emb]\n        if vision_emb is not None: embeddings.append(vision_emb)\n        if audio_emb is not None: embeddings.append(audio_emb)\n        return torch.cat(embeddings, dim=-1)\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Context Window Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept**: Optimizing the context window size and structure for maximum model efficiency.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Techniques**:\n",
    "- Dynamic context window sizing\n",
    "- Attention span optimization\n",
    "- Hierarchical context management\n",
    "- Context sparsity techniques\n",
    "\n",
    "**Implementation**:\n",
    "```python\n# Context Window Engineering\nclass ContextWindowEngineer:\n    def __init__(self, base_context_size=8192):\n        self.base_context_size = base_context_size\n        self.adaptive_sizer = AdaptiveContextSizer(base_context_size)\n        self.hierarchical_manager = HierarchicalContextManager()\n        self.sparsity_optimizer = ContextSparsityOptimizer()\n    \n    def optimize_context(self, tokens, query_complexity, memory_constraints):\n        # Adaptive sizing based on query\n        optimal_size = self.adaptive_sizer.calculate_optimal_size(\n            tokens, query_complexity, memory_constraints\n        )\n        \n        # Hierarchical structure creation\n        hierarchical_context = self.hierarchical_manager.create_structure(\n            tokens[:optimal_size]\n        )\n        \n        # Apply sparsity optimization\n        optimized_context = self.sparsity_optimizer.apply(hierarchical_context)\n        \n        return optimized_context\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Vector Compression Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept**: Advanced techniques for compressing embedding vectors while maintaining semantic information.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Techniques**:\n",
    "- Quantization methods\n",
    "- Knowledge distillation\n",
    "- Random projection techniques\n",
    "- Low-rank approximation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Implementation**:\n",
    "```python\n# Vector Compression Engineering\nclass VectorCompressor:\n    def __init__(self, target_dim=256, compression_ratio=0.25):\n        self.target_dim = target_dim\n        self.compression_ratio = compression_ratio\n        self.quantizer = VectorQuantizer(target_dim)\n        self.distillation_model = KnowledgeDistillationModel(target_dim)\n        self.random_projector = RandomProjectionMatrix(target_dim)\n    \n    def compress_vectors(self, vectors, method='quantized'):\n        if method == 'quantized':\n            return self.quantizer.compress(vectors)\n        elif method == 'distillation':\n            return self.distillation_model.compress(vectors)\n        elif method == 'random_projection':\n            return self.random_projector.compress(vectors)\n        elif method == 'low_rank':\n            return self._low_rank_approximation(vectors)\n    \n    def _low_rank_approximation(self, vectors, rank=128):\n        # SVD-based low-rank approximation\n        U, S, Vt = np.linalg.svd(vectors, full_matrices=False)\n        reconstructed = U[:, :rank] @ np.diag(S[:rank]) @ Vt[:rank, :]
        return reconstructed\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
